  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "All tests now pass (2 of 2).\n\nThe bug was in `src/vat.js`. `withVat` used `Math.floor(pence * 1.2)`, which truncates. For 999p, 999 × 1.2 = 1198.8, so it returned 1198p instead of 1199p. The comment above the function says the result should be \"rounded to the nearest penny\", so I changed `Math.floor` to `Math.round`. That is a one-line change and I haven't committed it.\n\nI didn't change the test file. The test expects 1199 for an input of 999, and that is the correct value under the function's documented behaviour.",
